        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: যুক্তি",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "যুক্তি — jukti — \"an argument; reasoning\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "তোমার যুক্তিটা ভালো, কিন্তু এটা সব জায়গায় খাটে না। tomār juktiṭā bhālo, kintu eṭā sôb jāygāy khāṭe nā. Your argument is good, but it doesn't hold everywhere."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "যুক্তি (jukti) is Sanskrit yukti, a joining and so a reasoning that holds together (Monier-Williams). It is a reasoned case, not a quarrel: তর্ক করা is to argue, যুক্তি is what you argue with."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
